---
// Public record. The mockup called this Lexicon: talks, panels, rooms.
// Roles are stated as given.
// The Berlin congress stays in Upcoming until it happens, and already has its own page.
import '../styles/fraunces.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/400.css';
import '../styles/global.css';
import RoomNerve from '../components/RoomNerve.astro';
import RoomShell from '../components/RoomShell.astro';
import BrandText from '../components/BrandText.astro';

// Each record shows `text` on the card. A record may also carry `more`:
// an optional list of paragraphs. When present, `text` acts as a short
// teaser and a native <details> "Read more" opens the full piece in place
// (no JS needed). Records without `more` render exactly as before.
type LexiconRecord = {
  img: string;
  alt: string;
  date: string;
  title: string;
  text: string;
  more?: string[];
  link?: { href: string; label: string };
  meta: string;
  role: string;
};

// Future commitments, shown first. Move each one into `records` once it has happened.
const upcoming = [
  {
    when: '26–27 October 2026 · Berlin',
    title: 'AUTOMA Chem 2026',
    text: 'Chemical Automation and Digitalisation Congress. Opening panel: data and AI governance as the foundation for sustainable digital transformation in the chemical industry. Invited by BGS Group. The note opens after the talk.',
  },
  {
    when: '4 February 2027 · Online',
    title: 'DataNext Trust Summit',
    text: 'Panel discussion.',
  },
  {
    when: '13–14 April 2027 · RAI Amsterdam',
    title: 'EuroLab Live',
    text: 'Speaker.',
  },
];

const records: LexiconRecord[] = [
  {
    img: '/cabinet/datanext-speaker-card.jpg',
    alt: 'DataNext Agentic Summit 2026 speaker card for Eduardo Sopalda',
    date: '28 May 2026 · Online',
    title: 'DataNext Agentic Summit',
    text: 'A commencement speaker had just told graduates to “destroy AI.” A few days later, five of us spent the closing panel on a harder question: how do you govern systems that act without us, without killing what makes them worth governing?',
    more: [
      'Calling for destruction isn’t a position you can build anything on. The Luddites didn’t stop the industrial revolution; they just missed the chance to shape it. The real questions about AI are harder and more interesting. What happens when agents stop assisting us and start acting for us? Where does accountability live in an autonomous system? How do you keep humans meaningfully in the loop without turning governance into theater?',
      'That’s the territory we went into at DataNext Agentic, with Giuseppe Cicotti (Allianz), Nuno Valério (Merck) and Maxim Romanovsky (Deutsche Bank), guided by Mercedes Pantoja (Siemens Healthineers). Insurance, pharma, banking and specialty chemicals turned out to be building the same muscle in different vocabularies. Giuseppe put it as “assurance comes before insurance.” I kept pulling us back to data integrity and the humanist case for governance. Proportional governance, with a fast lane for low risk and real scrutiny where being wrong is costly, is what lets you move at all.',
      'Mercedes said something that stayed with me: governance starts with oneself, before the frameworks, the policies or any tooling. You can’t govern what you haven’t first examined honestly in yourself.',
      'Destroy AI? That’s not the answer. Understand it, govern it, shape it, hold it accountable, and earn its trust through the unglamorous work of building the right foundations. Thank you to Philip Bell for bringing us together. We need more rooms like that one.',
    ],
    meta: 'Agentic AI · Responsible innovation',
    role: 'Speaker · panelist',
  },
  {
    img: '/cabinet/madrid-data-trust-forum.jpg',
    alt: 'Spain Cybersecurity and Data Trust Forum 2026',
    date: '21 May 2026 · Madrid',
    title: 'Spain Cybersecurity and Data Trust Forum',
    text: 'A 5 a.m. flight, terrible airport coffee, and a room of policymakers, bankers, technologists and security people circling one question: how do you build lasting trust in a world that moves faster than regulation can breathe?',
    more: [
      'What I enjoyed most wasn’t consensus but the healthy friction. Data sovereignty, shadow AI, regulation, cyber resilience: everyone came at them from a different seat. If everyone in the room says the same thing, you’re not having a conversation, you’re attending a rehearsal.',
      'Olga Forné spoke about regulation not as a burden but as a distinctly European strength, a foundation for trust. I agree, and it deserves to be said louder. Good regulation isn’t a tax on progress; it’s part of the architecture that makes progress last. The head of governance at Banco de España reminded us this is a marathon, not a sprint. The Google voice in the room added that risk is real, but the seven plagues of Egypt are not a governance framework.',
      'The risks we can’t ignore were there too: European data on infrastructure governed by US law, local data centres that don’t mean local control, and encryption keys sitting in the same cloud as the data they protect.',
      'I still left hopeful. The paths differed, sometimes sharply, but the intention was the same: protect what matters, keep meaningful control, and build systems that deserve trust. Trust isn’t the nice-to-have at the end of the strategy deck. Trust is the business model.',
    ],
    link: { href: 'https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/trust-real-business-model-eduardo-sopalda-u6pcf', label: 'Read the full article on LinkedIn' },
    meta: 'Data trust · Digital sovereignty',
    role: 'Invited participant',
  },
  {
    img: '/cabinet/sigmoid-un-ballroom.png',
    alt: 'Eduardo and fellow roundtable participants in the UN Ballroom at Ten Trinity Square',
    date: '13–14 May 2026 · London',
    title: 'Sigmoid — A room that remembers',
    text: 'In 1946, delegates to the first UN General Assembly gathered in the UN Ballroom at Ten Trinity Square. Eighty years later, we sat in that same room, talking about agentic AI.',
    more: [
      'In 1946, delegates to the first UN General Assembly gathered in the UN Ballroom at Ten Trinity Square, people trying to agree on how a changed world should be governed. Eighty years later, over two days in May, we sat in that same room, around the same kind of tables, talking about another technology that’s changing the world: agentic AI.',
      'You could feel it. The room still felt like a place where important decisions take shape, and AI governance is one of them. No single company, regulator or expert will get it right alone. It takes people from very different seats (growth, revenue, supply chain, data, policy) sitting down to share what’s working, admit what isn’t, and work out answers together.',
      'We talked about agents only being as good as the data and context we give them, about keeping humans able to see and steer what agents do, and about governance as the thing that makes innovation trustworthy enough to scale rather than the thing that stops it. Conversations like this are where that work starts. Thank you, Sigmoid, for opening the room.',
    ],
    meta: 'Reimagine with AI · London',
    role: 'Roundtable participant',
  },
  {
    img: '/cabinet/kith-climate-workshop-article.jpg',
    alt: 'Field note artwork for the Kith Lab Claude Code and Climate workshop',
    date: 'Late February 2026 · Kith Lab',
    title: 'Claude Code × Climate',
    text: 'In about 35 minutes, Claude Code did what would normally take weeks of ESG work. I walked in expecting a smart demo and walked out thinking we’re much closer to a new operating system for climate work than most teams realise.',
    more: [
      'Invited by my friend Yvonne Espinosa, one of the founders of the Kith AI Lab, I watched Diego Espinosa, with Ben Hillier from Kith Climate, run a simulation: day one as a solo VP of ESG at a private equity firm, Q1 reporting season, no team. Working only through Claude Code, 150+ files turned into a fund tear sheet, a portfolio risk scorecard, a due diligence memo flagging a high-risk deal, and an investor deck.',
      'What struck me wasn’t the speed but the shift. Chat helps you think and write; this helps you operate. It inferred the work plan, computed the numbers in code instead of guessing them, and reused each output as scaffolding for the next.',
      'The answer to hallucinations was quality by design, not hope: deterministic code for the maths, checks from different angles, and the saved time spent on verification. AI doesn’t remove the need to verify; it finally gives you the time to do it properly.',
      'My takeaway as someone in governance: if every concern becomes a roadblock, people won’t slow down, they’ll just move on without us. Climate professionals have a window to lead adoption with literacy, guardrails and a focus on outcomes. If AI compresses climate work from months to minutes, governance can’t stay quarterly and reactive either.',
    ],
    link: { href: 'https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/claude-code-x-climate-moment-ai-work-stopped-being-slogan-sopalda-pg2sf', label: 'Read the full article on LinkedIn' },
    meta: 'Climate · ESG · Agentic workflows',
    role: 'Invited workshop participant',
  },
  {
    img: '/cabinet/dama-management-summit-tour.jpg',
    alt: 'Data Management Summit Tour stop in Barcelona',
    date: '12 March 2026 · Barcelona',
    title: 'Data Management Summit Tour',
    text: 'Joined as a VIP guest of DAMA España for a conversation on data governance, quality, culture, and AI in organizations.',
    meta: 'Data management · DAMA España',
    role: 'VIP guest · attendee',
  },
  {
    img: '/cabinet/women-in-tech-talks.jpg',
    alt: 'Women in Tech Talks at dsm-firmenich',
    date: '18 September 2026 · dsm-firmenich',
    title: 'Women in Tech Talks',
    text: 'Introduced Yvonne Espinosa and Zainab Al Yasiri for a conversation on AI, confidence, curiosity, and trusting our judgment.',
    meta: 'Women in tech · AI · Leadership',
    role: 'Introducer',
  },
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Lexicon · EDUARDO sopalda</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <RoomNerve current="/lexicon" heading={false} />
    <RoomShell title="Lexicon" italic="out in the world.">
      <section class="open">
        <p class="kicker">Talks · panels · roundtables</p>
        <p class="display">The ideas I carry into rooms, and what those rooms give back.</p>
        <p class="dek">A living index of conversations across data, AI, trust, climate, and the human choices underneath them. Different rooms. Connected questions.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="next upcoming">
        <p class="kicker">Upcoming · not yet a record</p>
        <h2>Rooms ahead.</h2>
        <div class="up-list">
          {upcoming.map((u) => (
            <div class="up-item">
              <p class="when">{u.when}</p>
              <h3>{u.title}</h3>
              <p>{u.text}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <article class="feature">
        <figure>
          <img src="/cabinet/datanext-roundtable-recap.jpg" alt="Eduardo and fellow panelists at the DataNext Agentic Summit closing panel" />
          <figcaption>On the record · DataNext 2026</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">Featured · Agentic AI</p>
          <h2>Shaping the future of business with agentic AI.</h2>
          <p>At DataNext Agentic Summit, the closing panel was on opportunities, challenges, and what responsible innovation costs when systems move faster than approval.</p>
          <p class="meta">28 May 2026 · Online · Speaker, closing panel</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <section class="index">
        <p class="kicker">A field record · 2026</p>
        <h2>Conversations, indexed.</h2>
        <ol>
          {records.map((r) => (
            <li>
              <figure>
                <img src={r.img} alt={r.alt} />
              </figure>
              <div>
                <p class="meta"><BrandText text={r.date} /></p>
                <h3><BrandText text={r.title} /></h3>
                {r.more?.length ? (
                  <>
                    <p class="preview"><BrandText text={r.text} /></p>
                    <details class="more">
                      <summary>
                        <span class="more-closed">Read more</span>
                        <span class="more-open">Read less</span>
                      </summary>
                      <div class="more-body">
                        {r.more.map((para) => <p><BrandText text={para} /></p>)}
                        {r.link && (
                          <p class="more-link"><a href={r.link.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{r.link.label} ↗</a></p>
                        )}
                      </div>
                    </details>
                  </>
                ) : (
                  <p><BrandText text={r.text} /></p>
                )}
                <p class="meta"><BrandText text={r.meta} /></p>
                <p class="role"><BrandText text={r.role} /></p>
              </div>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </section>

    </RoomShell>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  html { overflow-y: auto; overflow-x: clip; }
  body { overflow-y: auto; overflow-x: clip; min-height: 100svh; color: var(--bone); }

  .kicker, .meta, .role, figcaption {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--champagne);
  }

  .display, h2, h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.08;
    color: var(--bone);
  }

  .display {
    margin: 0.8rem 0 0;
    max-width: 16em;
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 3.2vw, 3rem);
  }

  .dek, .feature p, .index p, .next p {
    max-width: 38rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--flesh);
  }

  .dek { margin: 1rem 0 0; }

  .feature {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(12rem, 18rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1.8rem;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 3.2rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(243, 235, 224, 0.14);
  }

  figure { margin: 0; }
  img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 16rem;
    object-fit: contain;
    object-position: center;
    background: #070707;
    border: 1px solid rgba(170, 104, 66, 0.4);
  }

  figcaption { margin-top: 0.55rem; }

  h2 { margin: 0.55rem 0 0.8rem; font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 2.4vw, 2.2rem); }
  h3 { margin: 0.3rem 0 0.35rem; font-size: 1.45rem; }

  .feature .meta, .index .meta { margin-top: 0.7rem; font-style: normal; font-family: var(--font-mono); }

  .index { margin-top: 4.5rem; }
  ol { list-style: none; margin: 1.2rem 0 0; padding: 0; }
  li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 8.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1.3rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 1.15rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(243, 235, 224, 0.14);
  }
  li img { height: 11rem; }
  .role {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    padding-top: 0.15rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(170, 104, 66, 0.7);
    color: var(--bronze);
  }

  /* Optional long text on a record: teaser + native "Read more". */
  .more { margin: 0.2rem 0 0; }
  .more summary {
    display: inline-block;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0.2rem 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--champagne);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(230, 203, 155, 0.45);
    transition: color 0.2s var(--ease), border-color 0.2s var(--ease);
  }
  .more summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .more summary::marker { content: ''; }
  .more summary::after { content: ' +'; }
  .more[open] summary::after { content: ' −'; }
  .more summary:hover { color: var(--gold); border-color: var(--gold); }
  .more summary:focus-visible { outline: 1px solid var(--gold); outline-offset: 3px; }
  .more-open, .more[open] .more-closed { display: none; }
  .more[open] .more-open { display: inline; }
  .more-body { margin-top: 0.4rem; }
  .more-link a { color: var(--gold); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  /* Where the browser lets <details> lay out its parts, put "Read less"
     under the full text. Older engines simply keep it on top. */
  .more[open] { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .more[open] summary { order: 2; align-self: flex-start; margin-top: 0.2rem; }
  .more-body p:first-child { margin-top: 0.6rem; }
  /* Once open, the full text replaces the teaser so nothing repeats. */
  li:has(.more[open]) .preview { display: none; }
  li:has(.more[open]) { align-items: start; }

  .up-list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(14rem, 1fr)); gap: 1.6rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .up-item h3 { margin: 0.4rem 0 0.4rem; font-size: 1.35rem; }
  .up-item p { margin: 0; }
  .next {
    margin-top: 3.2rem;
    padding: 1.6rem 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(170, 104, 66, 0.55);
  }
  .when {
    font-style: normal !important;
    font-family: var(--font-mono) !important;
    font-size: 0.72rem !important;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold) !important;
  }
  .links { font-style: normal; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .links a { color: var(--champagne); text-decoration: none; }
  .links a:hover { color: var(--gold); }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .feature, li { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    img, li img { height: auto; max-height: 16rem; }
  }
</style>
